        "text": "For Kotlin Compose (specifically Jetpack Compose and Compose Multiplatform), libraries for \"box and arrow\" or \"node-based\" diagrams are still in early stages compared to the mature web ecosystem (like React Flow). However, there are"
      }, {
        "text": " a few promising options depending on whether you need a **node editor/diagram** or a **statistical chart**.\n\n### "
      }, {
        "text": "1. For Node Editors \u0026 Flow Diagrams (\"Box and Arrow\")\nIf you are looking to build a flowchart editor, a node-"
      }, {
        "text": "based visual scripting tool, or a directed graph, there is no single \"standard\" production-ready library yet. The community"
      }, {
        "text": " mostly relies on custom implementations using `Canvas`.\n\n*   **ComposeFlow (Experimental)**:\n    *   **Description"
      }, {
        "text": "**: Created by GitHub user `thagikura`, this is an AI-first visual editor for building Compose apps. It features"
      }, {
        "text": " a **drag-and-drop visual node editor** interface.\n    *   **Status**: Open-source, early"
      }, {
        "text": " stage.\n    *   **Relevance**: While it is a full \"App Builder,\" the core visual editor uses"
      }, {
        "text": " exactly the \"box and arrow\" mechanics you are likely looking for. It is a good reference implementation for how to handle"
      }, {
        "text": " node connections, dragging, and zooming in Compose.\n    *   **Link**: [GitHub - ComposeFlow](https://github."
      }, {
        "text": "com/ComposeFlow/ComposeFlow) (Related to the \"KNodeFlow\" project mentioned in community discussions).\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "*   **Bonsai (Tree Views)**:\n    *   **Description**: A multiplatform tree view library"
      }, {
        "text": " for Compose.\n    *   **Relevance**: If your \"graph\" is strictly hierarchical (parent-child), this"
      }, {
        "text": " is a production-ready solution for file-explorer style \"box\" structures, though it lacks \"arrows\" and free"
      }, {
        "text": "-form positioning.\n    *   **Link**: [GitHub - adrielcafe/bonsai](https://github.com/"
      }, {
        "text": "adrielcafe/bonsai)\n\n*   **Build Your Own (Common Approach)**:\n    *   Most"
      }, {
        "text": " developers currently use the standard **`Canvas`** composable.\n    *   **Logic**: You can use a non"
      }, {
        "text": "-UI graph algorithm library (like a Java port of **JGraphT** or **GraphViz**) to calculate X"
      }, {
        "text": "/Y coordinates for your nodes.\n    *   **Drawing**: Pass those coordinates to `Canvas` to draw `draw"
      }, {
        "text": "Path` (cubic bezier curves) for arrows and standard Composables (via `Layout` or `Box`) for the nodes"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n\n### 2. For Statistical Charts (Bar, Line, Pie)\nIf by \"graph\" you meant data"
      }, {
        "text": " visualization, these are the most recommended and maintained libraries:\n\n*   **Vico** (Top Recommendation):\n    "
      }, {
        "text": "*   **Features**: Lightweight, highly customizable, supports Compose Multiplatform (Android, iOS, Desktop). Excellent for line"
      }, {
        "text": ", bar, and stacked charts.\n    *   **Link**: [GitHub - patrykandpatrick/vico]("
      }, {
        "text": "https://github.com/patrykandpatrick/vico)\n\n*   **Y-Charts**:\n    *   **"
      }, {
        "text": "Features**: A pure Jetpack Compose chart library that is easy to use for standard line, bar, and pie charts."
      }, {
        "text": "\n    *   **Link**: [GitHub - codeangi/YCharts](https://github.com/codeangi/YCharts"
      }, {
        "text": ") (Note: Verify the specific fork/maintainer as several exist).\n\n*   **KoalaPlot**:\n    "
      }, {
        "text": "*   **Features**: Specifically designed for **Compose Multiplatform**. It’s a great choice if you need your charts to work"
      }, {
        "text": " on Desktop/Web/iOS as well as Android.\n    *   **Link**: [GitHub - KoalaPlot](https://"
      }, {
        "text": "github.com/KoalaPlot/koalaplot-core)\n\n### Summary\n*   **For Flow"
      }, {
        "text": "charts/Nodes**: Check out **ComposeFlow** for reference, but expect to write custom `Canvas` code for a"
      }, {
        "text": " production feature.\n*   **For Data Charts**: Use **Vico**."
